{"id":17935,"name":"Kalamazoo County","slug":"kalamazoo-county","state":"Michigan","code":"MI","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/michigan-tax-deed-sales-property-deals-90-off/kalamazoo-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-20T14:50:35","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Deed Sale","typicalSaleDate":"The initial auction varies; the second auction in October​","bidProcedure":"Premium Bid","deposit":"$1,000","redemptionPeriod":"No redemption period for tax deed sales in Michigan​","extra":[{"label":"Auction Site","value":"Tax-Sale.info"},{"label":"County Website","value":"Kalamazoo Michigan County Government"},{"label":"Sale Contact","value":"Office of the Treasurer, Kalamazoo County, MI. Phone: (269) 384-8124. Kalamazoo County Treasurer"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed aligncenter is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"6P5EkOg0SjMresyp8Hf3lKQILXhoq1ZavTGcCNtYzVdnF79b24JwuBRAWDmiU\"><iframe title=\"Achieve Unbeatable 40-90% Off Deals - Kalamazoo County - Michigan Tax Deed Investing\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/bli0wZ02Fsg?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Achieve-Unbeatable-40-90%-Off-Deals---Kalamazoo-County---Michigan-Tax-Deed-Investing\">Unbeatable 40-90% Off Deals in Kalamazoo County, Michigan</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Want to cut your property investment costs dramatically? Kalamazoo County, <a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/michigan-tax-deed-sales-property-deals-90-off/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Michigan&#8217;s</mark></a> tax foreclosure sale can help you secure properties for 40% to 90% off their value. The auction opens each year and offers properties foreclosed due to unpaid taxes. You can find all the details about the auction rules and the properties on offer at Tax-Sale.info​.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-how-to-get-started-in-kalamazoo-county-tax-sale\">How to Get Started in Kalamazoo County, Tax Sale:</h2>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"1\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Registration</strong>: First, you&#8217;ve got to register. Make sure you do this at least 48 hours before the auction kicks off. Remember, you need to pay a $1,000 deposit via credit card or certified funds.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Auction Types</strong>: The auction has two main types:\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Live Bidding</strong>: You can actively increase your bid in real time.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Sealed Bidding</strong>: Submit your best offer without knowing other bids; the highest bid wins.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Payment</strong>: After winning, you have five business days to pay in full. Choose from several payment methods, but don&#8217;t delay; if payment falls through, you lose both the deposit and the property.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Important-Details\">Important Details to Note in Kalamazoo County Tax Deed Sale</h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n<div class=\"